  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\n\nHarvest issue #934 collected three reports of one defect in `backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/__tests__/lifecycleAdapter.test.ts` (PR #920 line 261, PR #920 line 267, PR #920 line 270): `failEventsFor(...statuses: string[])` interpolates its arguments, wrapped in hand-written single quotes, into a `CREATE TRIGGER … EXECUTE FUNCTION` statement. DDL cannot take bind parameters, and every caller passes the literals `\"done\"` or `\"error\"`, but the signature accepts any string, so a value containing a quote would break or inject into the SQL.\n\n## Task\n\nIn `lifecycleAdapter.test.ts`, change the parameter type of `failEventsFor` from `string[]` to an array of a literal union of the terminal statuses it is called with (`\"done\" | \"error\"`), so only those values can reach the interpolated SQL.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/__tests__/lifecycleAdapter.test.ts\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nThe signature change; call sites keep passing `\"done\"` and `\"error\"` unchanged.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nEvery other finding of harvest issue #934 and anything adjacent to the lines named in the Task, even in the same file.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `failEventsFor(\"x'y\")` does not type-check (`tsc` reports it), while the existing calls with `\"done\"` and `\"error\"` still compile and the file's tests pass.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=920 key=aa76f16603 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=920 key=8cc3c7f6d0 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=920 key=700b4387f8 -->",
